    "b": "Create one exquisite 3D medical atlas illustration for a professional radiology lesson specifically about \"{subject}\". Infer the correct anatomical region and disease/procedure from the full subject. Depict one coherent anatomically plausible relevant organ/equipment composition, with one finely detailed enlarged inset only if it clarifies the specific concept. Match the supplied CAA illustration's high-quality sculptural ivory/blush tissue, restrained plum/coral/teal accents, fine vessels and soft studio lighting. For technique topics show the actual imaging equipment/physical principle, not irrelevant brain anatomy. Full subject visible with generous margins, wide clean composition, genuinely transparent background. No text, labels, letters, numbers, arrows, badges, icons, grids, cartoon shapes or gratuitous gore. Conceptual educational artwork, never a fake diagnostic scan.",
    "c": "Create one sophisticated 3D medical atlas header illustration for a professional radiology lesson specifically on \"{subject}\". Identify the correct anatomical region and precise disease/procedure from this full topic. Show one coherent anatomically plausible organ/equipment composition expressing its characteristic concept, at most one finely detailed enlarged inset if educationally useful. Match the supplied CAA reference's premium sculptural ivory/blush tissue, restrained plum/coral/teal accents, fine texture and soft lighting. For imaging technique topics depict the relevant equipment/physical principle, not irrelevant anatomy. Genuinely transparent background, clean silhouette, wide composition, full subject visible and generous padding. No words, text, labels, letters, numbers, arrows, badges, icons or diagram grids. No cartoon or gratuitous gore. Conceptual medical illustration, never a fake diagnostic scan."
